---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Runtime"
  description="Understand how the durable runtime consumes the mdbase event/action interoperability profile."
  current="runtime"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero__inner">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow"><i></i> Runtime profile 0.1</p>
        <h1>Durable execution builds on interoperability.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="page-hero__aside">
        <p>
          The event/action profile defines portable messages and provider
          resolution. The runtime adds journals, scheduling, retries, and
          recovery without inventing a second contract system.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/interop/">Interoperability profile</a>
          <a class="button" href="/implementations/">Implementation profiles</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Four related layers</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div>
          <h3>Collection semantics</h3>
          <p>
            Loading, typing, validation, CEL queries, links, saved views,
            revision-safe mutations, lifecycle policy, and watching. These
            behaviors operate directly on the collection.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div>
          <h3>Event/action interoperability 0.1</h3>
          <p>
            CloudEvents envelopes, exact contract evidence, role declarations,
            boundary validation, and one-provider action resolution. The
            browser-safe reference bridge implements this layer.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div>
          <h3>Workflow execution 0.1</h3>
          <p>
            Durable journals, idempotent actions, timers, recovery, and
            provider-neutral execution. The Rust <code>mdbase-runtime</code>{" "}
            crate implements this execution layer with in-memory, SQLite, and
            PostgreSQL storage.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div>
          <h3>Connect embedding</h3>
          <p>
            Connect compiles exact application grants into transport behavior,
            supplies local or hosted collection authorities, and routes
            notification signals. It can bind the same portable envelopes
            durably without becoming mandatory for local applications.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Conformance profiles</h2>
    <p>
      Conformance uses atomic profiles. Interoperability bridges claim{" "}
      <code>event_action_interop/0.1</code>. Durable workflow engines add{" "}
      <code>workflow/0.1</code> after publishing shared fixture evidence.
    </p>
    <table class="profile-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Profile</th>
          <th>Covered behavior</th>
          <th>Separate profiles</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>event_action_interop/0.1</code></td>
          <td>CloudEvents, declarations, validation, authorization boundaries, multicast, and action resolution</td>
          <td>Workflow syntax, scheduling, retries, persistence, or recovery</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>runtime_contracts/0.1</code></td>
          <td>Legacy runtime-host behavior during migration to the interoperability substrate</td>
          <td>The portable event/action profile and durable execution evidence</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>workflow/0.1</code></td>
          <td>Durable workflow execution, action idempotency, timers, and recovery</td>
          <td>All collection semantics unless separately claimed</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>watch</code></td>
          <td>Real collection event delivery and ordering</td>
          <td>Runtime provider or workflow behavior</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
